ton but it just doesn't make  sense because it's meant to be as cheap  as possible and they literally just  bumped it up to a ten point two inch  display  about eight months ago so I'm sure that  this 10.8 inch iPad rumor is also  talking about the iPad air so which one  is it ten point eight or eleven well get  ready for this one we think is actually  both and let me explain why when the 11  inch 2018 iPad pro came out with a brand  new design the iPad air 3 was built with  the ipad pro's old 10.5 inch design  now what if Apple does this again  imagine the iPad air for being built  with a 2018 11 inch iPad pros design  this would mean that it would come with  support for the Apple pencil 2 in its  wireless charging feature the new modern  square edge design and the new rounded  corner display but Apple has to be very  careful because they can't make it so  good that people stop buying the iPad  pro so how can they achieve this well  instead of having an 11 inch display it  would come with a ten point eight inch  display  so both the eleven and ten point eight  is rumors would make sense at the same  time if the chassis was identical to the  iPad pro but the display itself was  slightly smaller if you think about it  the 11 inch iPad pro introduced a brand  new one point four three two one aspect  ratio so if the new iPad air maintains  the same old four by three aspect ratio  then the display size could actually be  ten point eight inches while using the  same exact metal chassis it would just  have slightly larger vessels on the top  and bottom of the display so this would  make the new ten point eight inch iPad  air look modern and appealing but the  display on the iPad pro would be slimmer  and look better  however there still needs to be some  more differences to make the iPad pro  worth the extra $300 on top of the new  iPad air so I think the air is gonna  come with the less powerful a13  processor which keep in mind is already  in every single new iphone including the  iPhone se making a cheaper since they  can mass-produce it on a higher scale  it's also not gonna have 120 Hertz  promotion display technology it's not  gonna have quad speakers it's not gonna  have the new light  scanner or the new ultra wide camera  it's not gonna have 600 nits of display  brightness and it's not gonna have  studio quality microphones all of those  features are reserved for the iPad pro  and those differences alone are gonna  make it worth spending an extra three  hundred dollars for the iPad pro if you  can afford it but at the same time the  newer square-edged design on the iPad  air is gonna make it really appealing  compared to the budget iPad options  pushing more people toward the new iPad  air now there are a few features that  I'm not totally sure about there's a  chance it'll come with face ID and  there's a chance that it'll come with a  brand new under display fingerprint  sensor and there's also a chance it'll  come with a USB C port but it might even  come with the old lightning port to  differentiate it a bit more so I'm not  completely sure about these two features  but what I do know for sure is that if  the new iPad air shares the same chassis  as the current 11 inch iPad pro then it  is a hundred percent going to support  the new magic keyboard case the reason  this makes sense for Apple is because  the keyboard case likely has very high  profit margins so even if someone spent  less money and chose the iPad air over  the pro Apple can later sell them on a  magic keyboard case and make that  difference back and if you've seen my  video on why that magic keyboard case is  Apple's master plan then you'll know  that Apple wants as many of these  keyboard cases in the hands of buyers as  possible since the magic keyboard and  its unique floating iPad design is meant  to be a symbol of the Apple brand so  there you have it we get an iPad air  that looks fresh and modern making  people want to spend more money on an  iPad purchase while also not being good  enough to cannibalize that our iPad pro  sales and the cherry on top is the magic  keyboard case support to help Apple make  some extra profit after the fact now  there are some rumors about this iPad  air getting a mini LED display but I can  almost guarantee that no iPad is getting  this display before the iPad pro gets it  first and that probably won't happen  until 2021 and then only after that we  can expect the rest of the iPad lineup  to  the new mini LED display so the whole  point of this video is that if you're  thinking about buying either the budget  iPad the iPad Mini or the iPad air  you should totally stop and wait for the  new iPad air but if you're interested in  the iPad pro go ahead and order one  right now since the iPad air is still  going to be missing a lot of the pro  features and if you do decide to go with  the pro we'll have links down below in  the description to the best deals on the  pro models so go ahead and tap the like  button and click the circle above to  subscribe if you want to see more videos  like this one thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next one  [Music]

